CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260414T180726Z
DESCRIPTION:Adults\, youth\, and children are invited join us to share in 
 A Thrill of Hope!\n\nAdvent begins in a weary world\, fractured by divisi
 on and despair. Yet across generations\, humanity has clung to the hope o
 f restoration\, and God continues to draw near. The Messiah has saved us\
 , is saving us\, and will save us. Suffering is not the final word. As we
  journey through Advent\, Christmas\, and Epiphany\, we watch for God's s
 aving work all around us: healing where there is hurt\, courage where the
 re is fear\, hope where there is despair. The miracle of Immanuel did not
  end in Bethlehem. The thrill of hope persists.\n\nWeekly Themes:\nFirst 
 Sunday of Advent: Keep Awake\nMark 13:24-37\nSecond Sunday of Advent: Pre
 pare the Way\nMark 1:1-8\nThird Sunday of Advent: Among You Stands One\nJ
 ohn 1:6-8\, 19-28\nFourth Sunday of Advent: Let It Be with Me\nLuke 1:26-
 38\nChristmas: Good News of Great Joy\nLuke 2:1-14 (15-20)\nFirst Sunday 
 after Christmas: My Eyes Have Seen Your Salvation\nLuke 2:22-40\nEpiphany
 : Another Road\nMatthew 2:1-12
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270110T094500
DTSTAMP:20261109T181142Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261129T094500
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T181142Z
LOCATION;X-BEDEWORK-UID=18832edc-1b27e154-011b-2819e770-00000021:Divinity 
 School
