CREATED:20261104T204605Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>To mark the Centennial of Duke University Press (DUP)\, DUP
  and the John Hope Franklin Humanities Institute (FHI) are jointly hostin
 g the second event in the 2026 series\, Publishing Fundamentals. This sym
 posium will feature two panels - one on editing academic journals and the
  other on book publishing in Black Studies - as well as a lunchtime netwo
 rking opportunity with DUP editors for junior faculty.\n<ul><p>Schedule:\
 n<p><li>10:00 am: Coffee and registration\n<p><li>10:30 am-12:00 pm: Firs
 t panel on academic journals\n<p>Moderator:\n<p>- Rob Dilworth\, Duke Uni
 versity Press\n<p>Panelists:\n<p>- Elizabeth Wilson\, Emory University\n<
 p>- Michael Hardt\, Duke University\n<p>- Priscilla Wald\, Duke Universit
 y\n<p>- Peter Sigal\, Duke University\n<p><li>12:00 pm-1:30 pm Lunch\n<p>
 <li>1:30 pm-3:00 pm: Second Panel on publishing Black Studies\n<p>Moderat
 or:\n<p>- Chris Ouma\, Duke University\n<p>Panelists:\n<p>- Tamura Lomax\
 , Michigan State University\n<p>- Sarah Cervenak\, University of North Ca
 rolina\, Greensboro\n<p>- Hugo ka Cahnam\, University of South Africa\n<p
 >- Celina de Sá\, University of Texas\, Austin\n<p><li>3:00 pm-4:00 pm: R
 eception</ul>\n<p>This event is generously co-sponsored by the Office for
  Research & Innovation and Office for Faculty Advancement at Duke Univers
 ity. We would also like to thank our departmental co-sponsors in the arts
 \, humanities\, and interpretive social sciences.\n<p>RSVP <a href="https
 ://duke.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bJaz1EC1th49CXI">here</a>\n<p>Parking f
 or event attendees is available at the Campus Drive parking lot located o
 n Anderson St across from the Rubenstein Arts Center. Spaces are limited 
 to 50.\n\nHourly public parking is also available at Sarah P. Duke Garden
 s. More information on parking and payment can be found <a href="https://
 gardens.duke.edu/visit/parking/">here</a>.
DURATION:PT6H
