DESCRIPTION:The Department of Chemistry is excited to host Prof. Hans Rena
 ta (Rice University) on Tuesday\, December 1\, 2026\, for a departmental 
 seminar. \nBy virtue of their unrivaled selectivity profiles\, enzymes po
 ssess remarkable potential to address unsolved challenges in chemical syn
 thesis. The realization of this potential\, however\, has only recently g
 ained traction. Recent advances in enzyme engineering and genome mining h
 ave provided a powerful platform for identifying and optimizing enzymatic
  transformations for synthetic applications and allowed us to begin formu
 lating novel synthetic strategies and disconnections. This talk will desc
 ribe our recent efforts in developing a new design language in chemical s
 ynthesis that centers on the incorporation of biocatalytic approaches in 
 contemporary synthetic logic. Case studies will focus on the use of this 
 platform in the chemoenzymatic syntheses of complex natural products. To 
 learn more about Prof. Hans Renata (Rice University) research\, please vi
 sit: https://ouri.rice.edu/people/hans-renata\n\n\nSeminar hosted by: Pro
 f. Edwin Alfonzo
DURATION:PT1H
