CREATED:20261117T160807Z
DESCRIPTION:AIM Photonics\, a Department of War Manufacturing Innovation I
 nstitute (DoW MII)\, offers end-to-end services spanning photonic integra
 ted circuits (PICs)\, interposers\, heterogeneous integration (HI)\, elec
 tronic-photonic design automation (EPDA)\, and packaging. AIM Photonics l
 everages the NY Creates Albany NanoTech Complex\, a 300 mm wafer fabricat
 ion facility in Albany\, NY\, and the Test Assembly and Packaging (TAP) f
 acility in Rochester\, NY\, to provide these state-of-the-art capabilitie
 s. As a DoW MII\, AIM Photonics' mission is to develop photonics and pack
 aging technologies\, make them available to the domestic ecosystem\, and 
 train a skilled workforce.\nThis talk will focus on how AIM Photonics is 
 advancing that mission. To help advance the ecosystem\, AIM Photonics off
 ers application-specific PIC technologies in 1) base telecom and datacom\
 , 2) SiN sensors\, 3) Quantum Flex (QFlex)\, and 4) III-V heterogeneous i
 ntegration. The base telecom PIC technology has been offered as an MPW si
 nce 2016 and is a feature-rich PIC platform. The SiN sensor platform is a
  SiN-only PIC platform with low-loss\, low-fluorescence waveguides and cl
 addings\, along with a thick oxide layer that isolates the substrate. The
  quantum technology is offered as both an MPW with quantum-enabled cells 
 for single-photon emission and detection and as the MEC Quantum Ultra Bro
 adband Photonic Integrated Circuit (QUPICs) platform. The III-V platform 
 features an integration path that includes hetero-epitaxially grown laser
 s.\n\nBIO: David Harame has served in various technology development and 
 executive roles throughout his career. David was an IBM Fellow and GLOBAL
 FOUNDRIES Fellow and served as CTO for RF Foundry Technologies for both c
 ompanies.  David is probably best known for his work on the development o
 f manufacturable Silicon Germanium\, HBT Bipolar and BiCMOS technologies.
  David is an IEEE Fellow. David Harame is currently the COO for AIM Photo
 nics.  In his current position he manages the AIM Photonics technology de
 velopment area including photonics\, heterogenous integration\, interpose
 rs\, test assembly and packaging\, and electronic photonic design automat
 ion.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261117T160807Z
